<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Cutting nodes to the clipboard</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="286" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Cutting nodes to the clipboard
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="489">
      <col width="234">
      <col width="237">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Use case: Cutting nodes to the clipboard</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Comment:</font></b> <font size="3">This case is similar to use case
            notes Copying nodes to the clipboard, except that the nodes and all links that go out
            or come in to them are eliminated.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="479">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Actor: User</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Normal course</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Alternative courses</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="162">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.When the type of editing is the selection of objects and there are
            only nodes selected, the user presses the key combination CTRL + X or chooses the
            option to cut that is available both in the main menu as in the standard toolbar or
            clicks on option from the popup menu of the node.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="162">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="143">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.The program copies in the clipboard the information of all selected
            nodes and all links that go out and come in to them, including the links that bind them
            to other nodes that are not copied. This information replaces the one that was stored
            in the clipboard.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="143">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="88">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.The option to cut that is in the main menu, on the standard toolbar
            and at the drop-down menu of the nodes is enabled.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="88">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="98">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.All the nodes and all links that go out or come in to some of the
            nodes selected are deleted.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="98">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="72">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.The nodes selected are deleted.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="72">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="101">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.The use case</font> <i><font face="Arial, sans-serif" size=
            "3">Updating the menus when changing the selected element</font></i> <font size="3">is
            executed.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="101">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="62">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.A new point to undo and redo the cut of the nodes is created.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="62">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="44">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">8.The use case <i>Updating menus when modifying a network</i> is
            executed.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="44">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">&nbsp;</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234" height="92">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">9.The network is marked as modified (if it was not already), placing an
            asterisk at the title of the window in which is being editing.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237" height="92">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
